cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "PFM: A Process Foundation Model with Reusable Process Representations for Predictive Process Monitoring"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of PFM, a process foundation model that learns a reusable event-state
  representation transferable across event logs and prediction tasks. Activities are represented by
  vocabulary-independent role embeddings derived from structural, temporal and positional features of
  directly-follows graphs, so a previously unseen log needs no update to the pretrained role encoder
  or causal transformer backbone; new prediction tasks are added as independently fitted lightweight
  heads.
